    Coder seat: Claude Opus 5 (max effort), per SOP Roles.
    
    Additive: one new public function in src/data/yaw_rotation.py. No edits to
    cylindrical_pose_features, invariant_conditioning, _orbit_average_batched,
    _orbit_average_loop, _rotated_variants, rotate_scene_metadata or
    resolve_frame_avg_cap.
    
    base = conditioner(metadata, device) on RAW Cartesian metadata (no cylindrical
    step); the orbit id set is POSE_KEYS (all four), each frame rotating depth and
    all four pose keys jointly via the existing _orbit_average_batched (angle-0
    base first, ascending angle order, declared chunk cap). context_audio and any
    other id come from the base pass; masks come from the base pass for every id.
    
    Two contracts are fail-closed and stricter than invariant_conditioning, which
    short-circuits instead: every POSE_KEYS id must exist in the conditioner output
    (averaging a subset would ship an undeclared treatment), and every sample must
    carry depth with one shared panorama width (a missing panorama would average
    four differently-posed views of one unrotated map). Depth is validated BEFORE
    the base pass so a mixed-width batch is reported by this contract rather than by
    the conditioner's own stacking.
    
    27/27 new tests green; regression subset (test_invariant_conditioning,
    test_yaw_symmetry, test_frame_avg_cap_config) 144/144 green.
    
