   687	    dimension into chunks of at most ``cap`` samples (default
   688	    :data:`FRAME_AVG_MAX_FWD_SAMPLES`; whole angles per chunk, so a chunk is
   689	    ``k * B`` samples), each chunk is one conditioner call, and the stacked output
   690	    is split back per angle. Terms are accumulated in the INPUT ANGLE ORDER
   691	    starting from the angle-0 base, so the additions are never reassociated: the
   692	    averaging arithmetic is identical to the loop.
   693	
   694	    ``cap_is_explicit`` only selects which knob the over-cap error names — the
   695	    module constant, or the config key that overrode it. A caller that hands us a
   696	    cap it read from a config must not be told to edit a module global.
   697	
   698	    What is NOT identical is the augmentation schedule under train-mode DINOv3:
   699	    its random RoPE rescale is drawn once per forward, so a chunk's angles share
   700	    a draw (see :data:`FRAME_AVG_MAX_FWD_SAMPLES` for the disclosure). In eval
   701	    mode there is no such draw and the two paths agree numerically.
   702	
   703	    Only the ``present`` (ViT) ids are re-run; masks come from the base pass.
   704	    A batch larger than the cap is rejected rather than silently exceeding it,
   705	    because a chunk cannot be smaller than one angle.
